Package: omx-clap-host
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: liblilv-0-0
Description: use CLAP plugins on a JACK rig, driven like mod-host
 omx-clap-host brings CLAP plugins, the modern open plugin format, into a
 live JACK or PipeWire rig. Each plugin runs as a JACK client with its own
 ports, and an instrument gets a MIDI input as well. Anything that already
 controls mod-host can control it over the same socket with the same
 commands. LV2 plugins run in it too, by their URI, through its LV2 to CLAP
 adapter, which loads lilv when the first one is added.
 .
 It comes with omx-clap-scan, which lists what is in a CLAP bundle and
 survives a plugin that crashes while loading.

Package: omx-clap-host-tests
Architecture: any
Depends: omx-clap-host (= ${binary:Version}), python3, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: fixtures to test a program that drives omx-clap-host
 Plugins and a signal source for testing a program that runs omx-clap-host as
 its CLAP worker: a plugin that reads the track information the host passes
 it, a compressor that reports meters, and a JACK client that plays a
 constant level. They are installed in /usr/libexec/omx-clap-host/tests, away
 from the directories CLAP hosts scan, and are of no use to anyone else.
 socket_conformance.py, beside them, checks how any server of the mod-host
 socket protocol splits what it receives into commands.

Package: libomx-clap-core1
Section: libs
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Pre-Depends: ${misc:Pre-Depends}
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: engine that runs CLAP plugins for omx-clap-host
 The library that loads and runs CLAP plugins: it checks a plugin before using
 it, activates and warms it up, keeps its parameters and saved state, and runs
 its audio on the thread of the program that hosts it. It knows nothing about
 JACK or sockets, so a program of your own can host CLAP plugins on it as
 well.

Package: libomx-clap-core-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: libomx-contract-dev (>= 3.1.0), ${misc:Depends}
Description: build a program that hosts CLAP plugins on libomx-clap-core
 What you need to write a program that hosts CLAP plugins on libomx-clap-core:
 the headers, the pkg-config file, the list of functions the library
 promises to keep, with the baseline each release is checked against, and
 the hosting limits as definitions in omx-contract's contract directory.

Package: libomx-clap-lv2-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: libomx-clap-core-dev (= ${binary:Version}), clap-headers, pkgconf, ${misc:Depends}
Description: run LV2 plugins in a CLAP host, as a library to link
 libomx-clap-lv2 lets a program that hosts CLAP plugins run LV2 plugins too:
 it presents one LV2 plugin as one CLAP plugin, with its controls as CLAP
 parameters, its latency, its own background worker and its default
 settings. It is a static library with its header and pkg-config file, and
 it loads lilv when the first LV2 bundle is opened, so a program that never
 opens one never needs lilv.
